Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

## 1. Before/After Every Test in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ClearAsync();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Before/After All Tests in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // Runs once before the first test in this class
        await SharedFixture.InitializeAsync();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // Runs once after the last test in this class
        await SharedFixture.DisposeAsync();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Some_Test() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 3. Once Before/After All Tests in the Assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StartAsync();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopServer(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        await WireMockServer.StopAsync();
    }
}
```

## 4. Once for the Entire Test Session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await EfCoreMigrations.ApplyAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

**Key points:**

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be | Context type |
|-------|-----------|---------------|--------------|
| Per-test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance | `TestContext` |
| Per-class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | **static** | `ClassHookContext` |
| Per-assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | **static** | `AssemblyHookContext` |
| Per-session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | **static** | `TestSessionContext` |

**Bonus:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (static, in any class) as a global cross-cutting hook that fires for *every* test in the run — handy for logging or tracing without modifying each test class. The context parameter and `CancellationToken` are both optional.
